  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Chen raises the target",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-yi-chia-chen-identity-0",
        "wire-2026-10-12-0402-arc-3-yi-chia-chen-extends-lead"
      ],
      "text": "Yi-Chia Chen has raised the leading public mark from 62.96 to 67.49 in a recorded overnight score event. Tufa Labs holds second at 56.52, leaving a 10.97-point gap. The event adds 4.53 points to Chen’s preceding recorded score; her individual midnight comparison is unavailable, so that figure is an observed improvement rather than a certified net morning gain. The higher target gives the chase a clear focus: Tufa is the nearest challenger, with mtg third at 45.00."
    },
    {
      "heading": "A tighter contest below the leaders",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-mark-barney-roster-1",
        "person-son-pham-roster-1"
      ],
      "text": "Son & Mark & Ronen gained 2.45 points against the morning baseline to reach 41.69 and climb from seventh to sixth, passing NVARC3 at an unchanged 40.97. Majkel1337 remains fourth at 42.66 and the last dance fifth at 42.55; the next positions are close enough that a modest improvement matters. A separate recorded event lifted 復活の混テキスト from 38.15 to 39.53, and the entry closes eighth, ahead of dreach.ai and AFF AI CLUB. That event is not a verified midnight net comparison. The observed Son & Mark & Ronen roster lists markbarney, scizical and sonphamorg; it does not assign credit for the score to an individual."
    },
    {
      "heading": "AFF’s earlier climb still matters",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-11-2158-arc-3-aff-ai-club-claims-gold-place",
        "wire-2026-10-11-2356-arc-3-aff-ai-club-enters-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-12-0158-arc-3-aff-ai-club-enters-gold"
      ],
      "text": "AFF AI CLUB’s move into the provisional gold places remains part of the story even though its 38.98 score did not rise in the morning comparison. The evening and overnight wire followed the earlier 5.06-point improvement and the reshuffle around it; this issue closes with AFF tenth. The public gold score line stays at 36.89. Lord Han Solo, seventeenth at 36.98, sits just 0.09 above that score threshold. These are public positions, with medals settled on the private board."
    },
